  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-Based TB Awareness, Detection, Diagnosis and Treatment in Mobility-Impacted Communities in Mon, Kayin, and Rakhine States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is currently covering all (10) townships in Mon State, and (4) Townships in Kayin State, namely, Myawaddy, Hpaan, Kawkareik, and Hlaingbwe, as well as (2) townships in Rakhine State (Buthidaung and Pauktaw) to address limited access to TB services of populations in hard to reach and conflict affected areas, and now covers a total population of 2,357,647.  IOM will implement a comprehensive package of TB and HIV integrated services and support focusing on increasing diagnosis and successful treatment amongst high risk and underserved population groups, specifically migrants, mobile populations and ethnic monitories living in underserved areas of Myanmar as envisioned in the NSP 2021-2025.</narrative>
  </description>
